gp-arcade-input 0
# The watchdog. A tilt during play hangs the game: the tilt check (the CTC
# channel 1 interrupt at 0158) feeds the watchdog while the switch is held,
# then on release jumps to itself with interrupts off. The watchdog runs out
# 16 frames later and resets the board, which tests its RAM again and goes
# back to attract mode. Then a coin, start 1 and a few seconds of play, to
# show the game runs on after the reset. The eighth column, X, is the tilt.
system rbtapper
columns CSRLDUTX
# power-on and attract mode
300 ........
# a coin, then start 1
6 C.......
54 ........
6 .S......
234 ........
# pour and send a drink
20 ......T.
40 ........
# tilt
6 .......X
# the hang, the watchdog's reset, the RAM test and attract mode
900 ........
# a coin and start 1 again, then play
6 C.......
54 ........
6 .S......
234 ........
20 ......T.
10 ........
6 .....U..
20 ......T.
100 ........
